# BartoszUP – always-on rules

Read `AGENTS.md` for full conventions. Key points:

- Django 5.2 modular monolith. Import direction (enforced by import-linter):
  `apps.listings` → `apps.profiles | apps.organizations` → `apps.accounts` → `apps.core`.
  `profiles` and `organizations` never import each other.
- Cross-app calls only via the lower app's `services.py`; permissions in `permissions.py`.
- Code/comments/commits in English; user-facing strings in Polish wrapped in gettext.
- No patient/health data features without an explicit task and ADR (GDPR art. 9).
- Before finishing: `uv run ruff format . && uv run ruff check . && uv run mypy . && uv run lint-imports && uv run pytest`.
- Model change ⇒ migration in the same commit + update `docs/domain-model.md`.
- Significant decision ⇒ new ADR in `docs/adr/`.
